    "id": "what",
    "title": "What JEVision is",
    "text": "A test in JEVision is a flowchart: a set of blocks joined by arrows. Each block is one step, such as “click the Sign in button”, “type the password” or “check that the inbox appears”. JEVision walks the arrows block by block. When something goes wrong, it tells you which block failed and shows you the screen at that moment. Every test is one JSON file on your disk. You can keep tests in git, review them in pull requests and run them in continuous integration, like any other code. You don't need to read or write JSON to use JEVision: the app draws each test, and you edit it on a canvas or by recording what you do."
