    "text": "It works with any app. JEVision needs no access to the app's code and no testing hooks inside it. If a person can use the app on a Mac, JEVision can test it. Anyone can read a test. A flowchart shows the path a user takes. A tester, a designer or a manager can follow it without knowing a programming language. Failures are easy to understand. Every run keeps a screenshot of each step, and for checks it shows the expected picture next to what the app actually showed. Small, clear changes. Test files are written in one fixed form, so every change shows up as a short diff that is easy to review. Free and open. JEVision is open source under the MIT license. Tests, screenshots and reports stay on your Mac. A screenshot leaves it only when a test uses an AI model in the cloud, for checks by meaning or to find an element described in words, or when you file a bug report on GitHub. The privacy policy describes what can leave your devices."
