    "text": "A board is a large canvas where you see your tests at a glance and lay them out your way. Boards are listed under Boards in the sidebar; click one to open it. All Tests appears by itself once the project has a test. It holds a card for every test, in a frame for each folder. New tests join it and deleted tests leave it on their own. Each card shows how the test last ran and when, and marks tests that are flaky or in quarantine (see Retries, flaky tests and quarantine ). A frame sums up its tests, for example “3 of 5 passed, 1 failed”. Dashed arrows lead to the tests a test runs; solid ones to the tests it needs to pass first. The app draws these arrows itself. To make a board of your own, click + next to Boards and type a name. Right-click an empty spot on a board to add: Add Test… : a card for a test that isn't on the board yet; Add Note : a note, written in Markdown; double-clicking an empty spot adds one too; Add Frame : a frame with a title; whatever lies inside it moves with it, and Fold shrinks it to its title; Add Link… : a web address; Add Image… : pictures from your Mac; you can also drag pictures onto the board or paste them; Add Link to Board : a card that opens another board, or a new one. The Command Palette ( ⌘ K ) has the same commands, such as Add Note to Board and New Board . Drag an item to move it. Select an item and drag its corner to resize it, or drag the dot beside it onto another item to draw an arrow. Double-click an item to open it: a test opens in the editor, a link in your browser. Right-click an item for more, such as Run , Show Blocks (the test's steps inside its card), Color and Remove from Board . Run All at the top runs every test on the board. Scroll to move around; pinch, or scroll while holding ⌘ , to zoom. Moved items snap to a grid; Snap to Grid at the top turns that off. ⌘ Z undoes a change. With an item selected, the keyboard works too: arrow keys pick the next item, Return opens it, R runs it, B shows or hides its blocks, C starts an arrow (then click where it goes), Delete removes it from the board. Right-click a board in the sidebar to Rename… it or Move to Trash . Links to a renamed board follow it. All Tests can be renamed but not deleted, and its tests can't be removed from it. Each board is a file in the project's boards folder, such as boards/All Tests.canvas , and pictures are copied into boards/images . Commit them along with your tests. The files use the open JSON Canvas format, so Obsidian can open them too."
