    "id": "blocks",
    "title": "Block types",
    "text": "The editor's block palette groups blocks by what they do: actions, waiting, checks, conditions and loops, sub-tests, data and system. Block Group What it does Arrows openApp Actions Opens the application under test, or another one, optionally with command-line arguments and environment variables next openFile Actions Opens files or web addresses next click Actions Clicks an element found by its picture, its description or accessibility, a point or the middle of an area, with any button, optionally holding ⌃ ⌥ ⇧ ⌘ next hover Actions Points at an element without clicking, optionally holding ⌃ ⌥ ⇧ ⌘ next drag Actions Drags from one place to another with any button, optionally holding ⌃ ⌥ ⇧ ⌘ next scroll Actions Turns the scroll wheel by lines or pixels, optionally holding ⌃ ⌥ ⇧ ⌘ next type Actions Types text, optionally into a field next pressKeys Actions Presses a key combination next waitFor Waiting Waits for something to appear or disappear, for the screen to settle, or for an interface element to be in a state next pause Waiting Waits a set time next check Checks Fails the test unless the screen matches a reference, or an interface element is in a state next if Conditions and loops Takes one of several ways depending on the screen, a value or an interface element then , elseIf1 …, else repeat Conditions and loops Runs its body a number of times body , next runTest Sub-tests Runs another test as one step next useData Data Runs its body once for every row of a CSV table body , next script Data and System Runs a script with typed inputs and outputs next clipboard Data and System Puts text or a picture on the clipboard, reads its text, picture or files into a variable, or checks its text next dateTime Data and System Keeps the current date and time, moved if you like, in a language and time zone of your choice, as a variable next http Data and System Sends a request to a web address, checks the answer and keeps parts of it as variables next database Data and System Asks an SQLite database file, checks the answer and keeps it as a variable next checkFile Data and System Waits until a file appears, disappears, changes or contains a text next command Data and System Runs a Terminal command, checks how it ended and keeps what it printed as a variable next In the tables below, every block also has type (its type name) and the arrow fields listed above. An arrow can be left out; a missing body is the only exception."
