    "text": "Brings the application to the front, moves the pointer over the middle of the window or over a target , and turns the scroll wheel. down brings what is further down into sight, whatever the Natural scrolling setting of the Mac. Recording joins turns of the wheel in one direction into one block, in lines from a mouse wheel or pixels from a trackpad. Field Required Value direction Yes \"up\" , \"down\" , \"left\" or \"right\" . amount Yes How far: a whole number from 1 to 10000. unit No \"lines\" (default), as a mouse wheel turns, or \"pixels\" , as a trackpad scrolls. at No A target to scroll over, such as one list of several. Default: the middle of the window. modifiers No Keys to hold down while the wheel turns, as for click : with \"cmd\" most applications zoom instead of scrolling. Default: none. waitForChange No true to wait, after scrolling, until the screen changes, and fail if it doesn't change within 10 seconds. Default: false . { \"type\": \"scroll\", \"direction\": \"down\", \"amount\": 5, \"unit\": \"lines\", \"next\": \"footer\" } { \"type\": \"scroll\", \"direction\": \"up\", \"amount\": 3, \"at\": { \"area\": \"0.2,0.2,0.6,0.6\" }, \"modifiers\": [\"cmd\"], \"next\": \"zoomed\" }"
