    "title": "Questions about testing",
    "text": "Which apps can I test? Any app on your Mac with a window: your own, someone else's, native or built with web technology. JEVision doesn't need the app's code or any changes to it. Do I need to know how to code? No. Record a test by using the app, and edit it on the canvas. The JSON file is there for those who want it. Do tests send my screen anywhere? Only checks by meaning send a screenshot to the AI model you choose, and you can choose a model that runs on your Mac. Every other check compares pictures on your Mac. Two things you turn on yourself also send a picture: email notifications show the screenshot of the failed step, and a bug report you file on GitHub includes the screenshots you choose. Private areas are painted over in both. Does it test iPhone apps or websites? JEVision tests Mac apps. A website can be tested in a Mac browser like any other app. The iPhone app is a remote for running tests on your Mac, not a way to test iPhone apps."
